      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2d38467f57433511425209|full_name}: people do it anyway, except instead they spam the api by deleting and remaking.  there's thousands of possible combinations for literally every of many times that in short name possibilities... there'd only be a little bit of squatting either way for very specific things.\n\nother platforms/games in the past have used solutions like having idle expiries (not in use or no activity) where they get re-rolled after a time, freeing up their prior number/name... or like discord where you can override it if you sustain your subscription (not my favourite method cuz it's not permanent).\n\nalso, 0000 and 0001 etc are just specific numbers that some people tend to overvalue, when there's numerous other interesting number combinations out there.",
